`Added`, `Fixed`, `Changed`, `Removed`
4. Outputs or updates `CHANGELOG.md` in Keep a Changelog format
5. If `CHANGELOG.md` already exists, prepends the new version entry

## Categorization rules
The script uses conventional commit prefixes and keyword matching:

| Prefix / Keyword | Category |
|-----------------|----------|
| `feat:`, `add:`, `added:`, `new:` | Added |
| `fix:`, `fixed:`, `bug:`, `hotfix:`, `patch:`, `resolve:` | Fixed |
| `chore:`, `refactor:`, `perf:`, `style:`, `docs:`, `ci:`, `test:`, `build:`, `update:`, `change:`, `changed:`, `improve:`, `tweak:`, `modify:` | Changed |
| `remove:`, `removed:`, `delete:`, `deleted:`, `drop:`, `deprecate:` | Removed |

Unmatched commits go into `Changed` as a safe default.

## Output format
```markdown
## [vX.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD

### Added
- Feature description (#PR)

### Fixed
- Bug fix description (#PR)

### Changed
- Change description

### Removed
- Removed feature description
```

